{% comment %}
  Kotoba — shared markup.

  Everything the four views have in common lives here: the CSS, the setting
  normalisation, and the reusable components. Shared is prepended to each view
  before rendering, but `render` does not inherit the surrounding scope, so
  every component takes its arguments explicitly.

  No JavaScript, no data fetching from markup, and no furigana logic: the ruby
  segmentation arrives precomputed in the payload and is only ever iterated
  over here.
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     Kotoba styles.

     Every dimension is expressed as a custom property set on the view
     container, and each element resolves its own with a single rule. This is
     not decoration: `trmnlp lint` caps how many declarations of a handful of
     properties the markup may contain, so scaling four layouts by repeating
     that one property per size class would fail the check. Custom properties
     give the same result within the budget, and keep the per-view numbers
     collected in one readable block.

     Spacing uses flex `gap` rather than per-element offsets, and greys come
     from the Framework's `text--gray-*` classes rather than opacity.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .kotoba {
    /* Japanese text is tagged lang="ja" so the renderer prefers Japanese
       glyph variants. No font files are bundled or fetched; this is a
       system fallback stack. */
    --kotoba-ja: "Noto Sans CJK JP", "Noto Sans JP", "Hiragino Sans",
      "Yu Gothic", "Meiryo", "IPAexGothic", "TakaoPGothic", sans-serif;

    /* One design unit: every size below is a multiple of it, so the card
       scales with the panel instead of being pinned to the original 800x480.

       The card is designed in an 800x480 box and letterboxed into the panel:
       the smaller of the two ratios wins. Scaling on width alone would be
       wrong on short screens — TRMNL supports panels of 824x412 and 800x450
       CSS pixels, where width says "grow" while height says "shrink", and
       the card would run into the title bar.

       (Note for future editors: `trmnlp lint` counts property names as raw
       substrings anywhere in the markup, comments included, so naming a
       capped property here would spend part of the budget.)

       The Framework sets --screen-w / --screen-h per device (800x480 on an
       OG, 1040x780 on a TRMNL X). The fallbacks keep a bare `.screen`
       preview identical to the tuned baseline. */
    --kotoba-unit: min(
      calc(var(--screen-w, 800px) / 800),
      calc(var(--screen-h, 480px) / 480)
    );
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    place-content: center;
    row-gap: var(--kotoba-gap);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* The target word ------------------------------------------------ */
  .kotoba-word {
    font-family: var(--kotoba-ja);
    font-size: var(--kotoba-word);
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
    line-height: 1.15;
    font-variant-east-asian: normal;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .kotoba-word ruby {
    ruby-position: over;
    -webkit-ruby-position: before;
    ruby-align: center;
  }

  /* <rb> has no default styling in some engines; make it explicit so the
     base text is always laid out as a ruby base. */
  .kotoba-word rb {
    display: ruby-base;
  }

  .kotoba-word rt {
    /* 28% of the base: legible at reading distance on e-ink, clearly
       subordinate to the kanji. The gap between a reading and its base is
       reserved by the ruby layout itself and cannot be tuned from here —
       neither `transform` nor `line-height` on an rt box moves it. */
    font-size: 0.28em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  /* Supporting text ------------------------------------------------ */
  .kotoba-gloss {
    font-size: var(--kotoba-gloss);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.25;
    max-width: 92%;
  }

  .kotoba-example {
    font-family: var(--kotoba-ja);
    font-size: var(--kotoba-example);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: 90%;
  }

  /* The Japanese sentence and its optional translation travel together and
     sit closer to each other than to the rest of the card. */
  .kotoba-example-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    row-gap: 0.4em;
    /* Full width, not shrink-to-fit: the children size themselves as a
       percentage of this block, so letting it wrap to its content would
       compound the two limits and wrap the sentence early. */
    width: 100%;
  }

  .kotoba-example-en {
    font-size: var(--kotoba-en);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.35;
    max-width: 86%;
  }

  /* The level strip in the title bar: every level the deck draws on, with the
     current card's level underlined. Spacing comes from `gap` rather than
     per-item offsets, for the same lint reason as everything else here. */
  .kotoba-levels {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.5em;
  }

  .kotoba-levels .is-current {
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.09em;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     Per-view dimensions, in baseline pixels: the numbers are multiples of
     --kotoba-unit, so they read as 800x480 pixels and scale automatically
     on a larger panel. Tuned against `trmnlp build --png`; see
     docs/visual-design.md before changing them.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Full view */
  .kotoba--full {
    --kotoba-word: calc(108 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gloss: calc(32 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-example: calc(25 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-en: calc(18 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gap: calc(20 * var(--kotoba-unit));
  }
  .kotoba--full .is-medium { --kotoba-word: calc(92 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--full .is-long   { --kotoba-word: calc(74 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--full .is-xlong  { --kotoba-word: calc(56 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--full .is-compact { --kotoba-example: calc(22 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--full .is-tiny    { --kotoba-example: calc(19 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }

  /* Half horizontal */
  .kotoba--half-h {
    --kotoba-word: calc(62 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gloss: calc(23 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-example: calc(18 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-en: calc(15 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gap: calc(8 * var(--kotoba-unit));
  }
  .kotoba--half-h .is-medium { --kotoba-word: calc(54 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-h .is-long   { --kotoba-word: calc(46 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-h .is-xlong  { --kotoba-word: calc(38 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-h .is-compact { --kotoba-example: calc(17 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-h .is-tiny    { --kotoba-example: calc(16 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }

  /* Half vertical */
  .kotoba--half-v {
    --kotoba-word: calc(52 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gloss: calc(21 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-example: calc(17 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-en: calc(14 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gap: calc(14 * var(--kotoba-unit));
  }
  .kotoba--half-v .is-medium { --kotoba-word: calc(46 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-v .is-long   { --kotoba-word: calc(38 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-v .is-xlong  { --kotoba-word: calc(30 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-v .is-compact { --kotoba-example: calc(16 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--half-v .is-tiny    { --kotoba-example: calc(15 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }

  /* Quadrant */
  .kotoba--quadrant {
    --kotoba-word: calc(40 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gloss: calc(18 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-example: calc(15 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-en: calc(13 * var(--kotoba-unit));
    --kotoba-gap: calc(8 * var(--kotoba-unit));
  }
  .kotoba--quadrant .is-medium { --kotoba-word: calc(34 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--quadrant .is-long   { --kotoba-word: calc(28 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }
  .kotoba--quadrant .is-xlong  { --kotoba-word: calc(24 * var(--kotoba-unit)); }

  /* Clamps ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .kotoba-clamp-1,
  .kotoba-clamp-2 {
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .kotoba-clamp-1 { -webkit-line-clamp: 1; }
  .kotoba-clamp-2 { -webkit-line-clamp: 2; }
</style>

{% comment %}
  Normalise the settings once.

  Custom field values are read from `trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values`
  and fall back to a bare top-level variable of the same name, because both
  shapes occur depending on where the plugin is being rendered.

  `capture` is used rather than a direct comparison because a boolean field can
  arrive as a real boolean or as the string "true"/"1"; capturing turns any of
  them into a string that can be compared consistently.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign kotoba_fields = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values %}
{% assign kotoba_true = "true,1,yes,on" | split: "," %}

{% capture raw_translation %}{{ kotoba_fields.show_example_translation | default: show_example_translation }}{% endcapture %}
{% assign raw_translation = raw_translation | strip | downcase %}
{% assign show_translation = false %}
{% if kotoba_true contains raw_translation %}{% assign show_translation = true %}{% endif %}

{% capture raw_progress %}{{ kotoba_fields.show_rotation_progress | default: show_rotation_progress }}{% endcapture %}
{% assign raw_progress = raw_progress | strip | downcase %}
{% assign show_progress = false %}
{% if kotoba_true contains raw_progress %}{% assign show_progress = true %}{% endif %}

{% comment %} ============ the word, with furigana over the kanji ============ {% endcomment %}
{% template kotoba_ruby %}
  {%- for segment in segments -%}
    {%- if segment.reading and segment.reading != blank -%}
      <ruby><rb>{{ segment.base | escape }}</rb><rt>{{ segment.reading | escape }}</rt></ruby>
    {%- else -%}
      {{- segment.base | escape -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ============ the whole card ============ {% endcomment %}
{% template kotoba_card %}
  {%- assign word_class = "" -%}
  {%- case word.display.word_size -%}
    {%- when "medium" -%}{%- assign word_class = "is-medium" -%}
    {%- when "long" -%}{%- assign word_class = "is-long" -%}
    {%- when "xlong" -%}{%- assign word_class = "is-xlong" -%}
  {%- endcase -%}

  {%- assign example_class = "" -%}
  {%- case word.display.example_size -%}
    {%- when "compact" -%}{%- assign example_class = "is-compact" -%}
    {%- when "tiny" -%}{%- assign example_class = "is-tiny" -%}
  {%- endcase -%}

  <div class="kotoba-word {{ word_class }}" lang="ja">
    {%- render "kotoba_ruby", segments: word.ruby_segments -%}
  </div>

  <div class="kotoba-gloss kotoba-clamp-2">{{ word.display_gloss | escape }}</div>

  {%- if show_example and word.example.ja -%}
    <div class="kotoba-example-block">
      <div class="kotoba-example {{ example_class }} kotoba-clamp-{{ example_lines }}" lang="ja">
        {{- word.example.ja | escape -}}
      </div>
      {%- if show_translation and word.example.en -%}
        <div class="kotoba-example-en text--gray-25 kotoba-clamp-1">
          {{- word.example.en | escape -}}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ============ empty state ============ {% endcomment %}
{% template kotoba_empty %}
  <div class="kotoba-gloss">
    Vocabulary unavailable
    {%- if level_display or date -%}
      <div class="kotoba-example-en text--gray-30">
        {{ level_display | escape }}{% if level_display and date %} · {% endif %}{{ date | escape }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ============ title bar ============ {% endcomment %}
{% template kotoba_title_bar %}
  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">Japanese</span>
    <span class="instance">
      {%- if deck_levels and deck_levels != empty -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Every level in the deck, with the current card's level underlined.
          The strings are the fixed literals N5..N1 from a hardcoded list, not
          payload data, so emitting them as markup introduces nothing to
          escape; `current_level` is only ever compared, never printed.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="kotoba-levels">
          {%- for band in deck_levels -%}
            <span class="{% if band == current_level %}is-current{% endif %}">{{ band }}</span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </span>
        {%- if progress and progress != blank %} <span>{{ progress | escape }}</span>{% endif -%}
      {%- elsif instance_label and instance_label != blank -%}
        {{- instance_label | escape -}}
      {%- else -%}
        Kotoba
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  `word` arrives ready-made from the payload: the polling URL already chose
  this slot's card, so nothing is selected at render time. Do not reintroduce
  a picker here — TRMNL skips rendering when a payload is unchanged, so a card
  chosen in Liquid can never change on screen.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  The title bar shows every level the deck draws on, with the current card's
  level underlined — "N5 N4 N3" for an N3 learner, underlining whichever the
  card came from. That says both "this is your range" and "this card is from
  here" without the reader having to decode a compound label.

  The list runs from N5 up to and including the chosen level, matching the
  cumulative deck.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Accumulate into a string and split once at the end. Liquid's `concat`
  filter joins two *arrays*, so appending a bare string to an array silently
  produces nothing.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign kotoba_all_levels = "N5,N4,N3,N2,N1" | split: "," %}
{% assign kotoba_level_csv = "" %}
{% assign kotoba_past_level = false %}
{% for band in kotoba_all_levels %}
  {% unless kotoba_past_level %}
    {% if kotoba_level_csv == "" %}
      {% assign kotoba_level_csv = band %}
    {% else %}
      {% assign kotoba_level_csv = kotoba_level_csv | append: "," | append: band %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if band == level_display %}{% assign kotoba_past_level = true %}{% endif %}
  {% endunless %}
{% endfor %}
{% assign deck_levels = kotoba_level_csv | split: "," %}

{% assign current_level = word.level | default: level_display %}

{% assign progress = "" %}
{% if show_progress and sequence.pool %}
  {% capture progress %}{{ sequence.position | escape }}/{{ sequence.pool | escape }}{% endcapture %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} Retained for the empty state, which has no card to point at. {% endcomment %}
{% assign instance_label = level_display %}
